1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,436
When ransomware takes a hospital's records offline, nurses go back to paper for days, sometimes weeks.

2
00:00:06,486 --> 00:00:11,707
Afterwards, every vital sign and every dose has to be typed back in.

3
00:00:11,757 --> 00:00:14,950
ClinBridge keeps that documentation digital, safe and offline.

4
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:18,728
It runs in Chrome on a ward laptop.

5
00:00:18,778 --> 00:00:21,089
This is fictional practice data.

6
00:00:21,139 --> 00:00:28,644
A nurse signs in with a PIN, and before charting, ClinBridge makes them confirm the patient:

7
00:00:28,694 --> 00:00:31,950
name, date of birth and record number.

8
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,164
An admin declares the outage.

9
00:00:35,214 --> 00:00:44,807
From now on the app blocks every cloud call, even one that was already running.

10
00:00:44,857 --> 00:00:49,950
AI may only run on the device itself.

11
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:53,796
Nurses keep charting as usual:

12
00:00:53,846 --> 00:01:05,335
vitals, medicines with a second-nurse check for high-alert drugs, notes, fluids, lab results and handovers.

13
00:01:05,385 --> 00:01:09,950
Everything is saved on this laptop.

14
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:12,501
Paper forms can be photographed.

15
00:01:12,551 --> 00:01:18,113
ClinBridge tries Gemini Nano on the device through Firebase AI Logic.

16
00:01:18,163 --> 00:01:25,256
On this laptop the hardware can't run Gemini Nano, and the app says so.

17
00:01:25,306 --> 00:01:30,358
It never falls back to the cloud during an outage.

18
00:01:30,408 --> 00:01:34,950
The nurse types the values beside the photo instead.

19
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:49,950
Records are encrypted at rest with AES-256, survive a restart, and every change goes into a tamper-evident audit chain.

20
00:01:50,000 --> 00:01:59,950
When the systems return, an admin checks the network and clears it.

21
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:04,950
Only now is cloud AI allowed.

22
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:16,929
In the recovery worklist, Firebase AI Logic gives each photo record a second look with Gemini in the cloud, protected by App Check.

23
00:02:16,979 --> 00:02:19,533
This is a live response.

24
00:02:19,583 --> 00:02:28,387
It lists where its reading differs from what the nurse typed, but it never changes the record.

25
00:02:28,437 --> 00:02:29,950
The nurse decides.

26
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:36,236
Checked records are exported as FHIR R4 for the EHR team.

27
00:02:36,286 --> 00:02:41,950
The export passes the official HL7 validator with zero errors.

28
00:02:42,000 --> 00:02:43,450
To be clear:

29
00:02:43,500 --> 00:02:45,950
cloud inference is tested live.

30
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:54,950
The on-device Gemini Nano path is built and tested with mocks, but not verified on real hardware yet.

31
00:02:55,000 --> 00:02:55,506
ClinBridge.

32
00:02:55,556 --> 00:02:59,950
Charting that keeps going when the EHR doesn't.
